It's Wednesday, March 11 in Australia and New Zealand, which means it's the official launch day for all of the products Apple introduced last week, including the new low-cost <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macbook-neo/">MacBook Neo</a>, the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-17e/">iPhone 17e</a>, the M5 Pro and M5 Max <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macbook-pro/">MacBook Pro</a> models, the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/studio-display/">Studio Display</a>, the &zwnj;Studio Display&zwnj; XDR, the M4 <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad-air/">iPad Air</a>, and the M5 <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macbook-air/">MacBook Air</a>.<br/>
<br/>
